 "transcription": {
  "from": "the published article (PDF). The pore solutions are printed only as the plots of Figs. 13-16; they are read from the vector drawing of those figures: the center of every marker, mapped to time and concentration through the major ticks of its panel, the legend telling the markers apart by shape and fill. Table 3 is read in the text layer and parsed row by row.",
  "checked_against_source": true,
  "note": "The major ticks of each panel lie on a straight line in log10 to within 5e-4 decades, and the drawing is written to 0.01 pt, so the reading adds less than 0.2 % to the values plotted; the authors give a standard deviation of 5 to 10 % for the analyses (Section 2.2, p. 1392). The ages are the eleven of Table 3; every marker lies within 0.005 decades of one. A value below the lower end of the concentration axis (0.01 mmol/L) is not plotted, and so not in the table: aluminum before 8 h or 1 day. Calcium is not plotted at 550 days in four of the pastes, and aluminum at 550 days in OPC-Qz. OH- is the free hydroxide the authors computed from the pH measured with an electrode calibrated against KOH solutions. S is total sulfur, analyzed by ICP-OES. The concentrations are printed to four significant digits."
